# Deploys the cross-restart replay-queue ordering fix AND restarts, which the
# previous deploy of this file deliberately did not do.
#
# Restarting normally costs the in-flight interval, because
# `recover_interrupted_deferred_replay` rolls any non-admitted marker back to
# its start. Here that cost is zero: the in-flight interval is
# jupyter-scientific-full:201344:262144, measured to need ~5.9 h of training
# against a ~1.26 h disk window, so it cannot finish and the rows are
# discarded either way -- and the rollback is what RECLAIMS the volume.
#
# Not restarting is the worse option, not the safe one: the disk floor is
# ~1.26 h away, DISK_EXHAUSTED_EXIT is 90 and the unit carries
# RestartPreventExitStatus=42 90, so the next halt stays halted.
#
# On this restart the recovery path records the stall, the queue reorders, and
# a smaller interval -- there are 131 unresolved, many 14,336-18,432 rows --
# gets the generation instead.

